# Property Intel — viewer rules (HTML/JS)

Single-file pages served by GitHub Pages at responder-intel.vyanet.com. No build step, no bundler. External libs via CDN (three.js) — test harnesses must stub CDN imports or modules never evaluate and every check silently passes.

## Versioning

Each viewer carries a `BUILD`/`VERSION` const near the top (element-review v6.8.6, viewer v2.9.4, responder-intel v2.5.2, hoa-viewer v2.3.3, plane-viewer v1.0.0, plane-test v0.2.0, nadir-geo 1.3.0; model-viewer is versioned via CHANGELOG/design doc, not in-file). Bump on every ship; element-review shows a build chip and stamps `version` into the critique payload. The critique payload is a compatibility contract: 19 keys, byte-identical across substrates except `substrate` — extend, never mutate or remove.

## Query param contracts (do not break; additions are fine)

- **element-review.html**: `site, site_no, addr, type, kind (school raises pin cap to 20), nadir (URL-ENCODED Static-Maps URL — georeference is scraped from its center/zoom), pins, catalog, key, round, rationale, route, view, map (0=flat fallback), sides (1=A/B/C/D labels, default off), margin (IGNORED as of v6.8.6), parcels, debug` + `center/zoom` override. `qp()` is a regex that stops at the first `&` — nested URLs MUST be encoded or `zoom`/`size` leak as top-level params.
- **model-viewer.html**: `property, view, model, dataRoot, alpha, azimuth, polar, ent_x, ent_y, autocapture (headless — v1-Pages usage SUPERSEDED), tab, debug, proxy` + live layer: `chekt (JWT fallback mode), chektdev, chektch, livems, gw (0 disables gateway)`.
- **viewer.html**: `property, mode, tab`. Record resolution everywhere: `?property=<hash>` → `data/index/{hash}.json` → `views` map → `data/{view}/{viewId}.json`; index 404 falls through to `data/drone-test/{id}.json`.
- Live-layer precedence (locked): explicit `&chektdev/&chektch` → token's own sub/channel → record's `live.device`.

## Catalog resolution

`data/pin-catalog/pins-catalog.json` — 239 pins `{id, name, definition, section, role: primary|concern, account_type: [residential|commercial], analysis: [fr|wf|shared]}`. element-review's add-search deliberately offers ALL 239 (an analyst may name any pin); satellite Pass 1 emits only the ranked twenty — that asymmetry is enforced server-side, never in the viewer. Match pins by id for identity, by NAME for derived-geometry lookups where a reviewer's dragged correction must win. Never edit the catalog to change pass behavior.

## Geometry invariants (each encodes a real incident)

- Map substrate: `tilt: 0`, `rotateControl: false`, `setTilt(0)` asserted — a Static-Maps nadir projects to an axis-aligned rectangle at every zoom ONLY under those conditions; one OverlayView sizes image + pins from one projected rectangle so they cannot drift apart.
- Google Maps pane stack is `mapPane → overlayLayer → markerLayer → overlayMouseTarget → floatPane`; the nadir `<img>` lives in `#nadirPane` inside mapPane; `#frame` must be in overlayMouseTarget for dragging. Know the stack before parenting anything.
- ALL polygon math in a local frame (`NadirGeo.localFrame`) — never on absolute projected metres (catastrophic cancellation; the winding-sign test only worked by luck).
- Geometry lives in `nadir-geo.js` (dependency-free, true Web Mercator) — never `google.maps.Projection`, so the basemap can swap (EagleView candidate). responder-intel.html's flat `pixelToLatLng` is a known defect (0.488% N-S stretch) — migrate it to nadir-geo, don't copy it. `shared.gs pixelToLatLng` is dead code with the same bug — never revive.
- Placement: reviewers pin anywhere on the captured nadir (no lot-distance wall as of v6.8.6). The 5–95% storable box is still refused with a toast — `clampCoords`-style silent relocation is the bug class, not a fix. Do not widen COORD_MIN/MAX without widening `clampCoords()` in shared.gs.
- Attach overlays at construction (`new Polygon({map})`), wrap optional/newer layers in try/catch with capability checks; in tests count only LIVE overlays (`o._map`).
- Static Maps: `size=` IS the logical size; `scale=2` only doubles pixel density — dividing moves the NW corner ~69 m.
- Sides convention: alpha = frontage bearing; bravo/charlie/delta = +90/180/270 CLOCKWISE (authority: model-viewer VIEW_OFFSETS). Side labels stay `ER_SIDES_DEFAULT=false` until satellite.gs supplies `&alpha=`.
- Headless/autocapture paths NEVER construct OrbitControls.

## Data ownership

Everything under `data/` is written by the Apps Script sync — a hand-edit (e.g. a camera `live` block) is overwritten on the next sync; proven twice. Viewer features needing new record fields require the sheet + sync change first. `config.js` is generated by the GitHub Action from a repo secret — never hand-edit. Records may reference three image hosts: CloudFront (current), Cloudinary (legacy drone-era), Google Static Maps (satellite).

## Verification before delivery (all required)

1. Extract the `<script type="module">` to a `.mjs` and `node --check` it.
2. Brace/paren balance + duplicate-declaration scan (regex comment-stripping fails on `//` in URLs — use a real parse or careful anchors).
3. Every `getElementById('x')` literal has a matching `id="x"`; every `onclick="fn("` resolves on window (this referee caught a shipped bug).
4. Scripted edits: exact-string replacement with an occurrence-count assert per block; anchor on ASCII-only strings (files contain 1,000+ non-ASCII chars, em-dashes in comments).
5. Playwright (chromium) behavioral pass with `page.route` stubs for CDN imports, `maps.googleapis.com` (hand-written google.maps stub with REAL pane divs + Mercator fromLatLngToDivPixel), `script.google.com`, and CHEKT endpoints. End-of-module probe = the last `window.*` assignment, not a bare function name.
6. Before patching a viewer, PROVE the local copy matches what is live (probe ~50 distinctive one-line strings + a declaration inventory) — local copies have been a generation behind before; patching blind silently reverts shipped work. The live site / GitHub HEAD is the reference.
7. State plainly anything not verified (e.g. "map render not verified — sandbox can't reach maps.googleapis.com"). Marked-up screenshots from the live page are the highest-value feedback — ask for them.
